Confidence bands quantify the uncertainty in a predicted survival curve, and conditional survival
gives an updated estimate that is directly meaningful for a patient already some time into
follow-up. Both are straightforward extensions of the base `predict()` call.

### Median survival time

A common clinical summary is the predicted median survival time: the earliest time at which the
survival curve drops to 0.5. Use `predict_median()` for a direct answer without having to inspect
the full curve.

::: {#456bbb59 .cell execution_count=27}
``` {.python .cell-code}
# Predicted median survival time for each subject
cox.predict_median(newdata, format="polars")
```

